Asseration: Asseration is a validation ponit. with help of Asseration we can verify the expected 
result. like title of page or some elemnt is disapled on webPage or not,or some properity on 
the web element.
To do that cypress mainly provide Two type of Asseration
1) implicit Asseration: these are the defult asseration in cypress 
under implicit will mainly used two things like Should,and. it's a two keyworked 
eq,contain,include, exist,have.lenght, have.value, not.eq, be,visible

2) Explicit Asseration : so to use these asseration we need to write explicitly: 
two keyworked mainly will useed expect (BDD),assert(TDD).
//
"Implicit wait is a global wait that tells Selenium to wait for an element while locating it. 
You can configure it in your common setup file or before starting your test execution.
Explicit wait is condition-based and waits for a particular condition, such as element visibility or 
clickability. I prefer explicit wait because it provides better control and flexibility."
Explicit Wait should be written inside the test or reusable method wherever you need to wait for a specific condition.
